{"cluster_id": "C-3550", "topic": "S3 staging fallback", "target": "configuration", "member_ids": ["B019-088", "B033-110"], "canonical_claim": "Review finding \u211631 is real: an explicit `staging_backend=s3` can silently fall back to local staging after a failed conditional-copy probe, unexpectedly consuming local disk and hiding a configuration mismatch. Additionally, Explicit `staging_backend=s3` can silently fall back to local staging after conditional-copy capability probing fails, hiding configuration errors and unexpectedly consuming local disk.", "issue_ids": ["\u211631"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-17-codex-review-triage.md#L461-L469", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-17-codex-review-triage.md#L50-L51", "docs/superpowers/reports/20260717_codex_review.md#major-severity"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3551", "topic": "configuration", "target": "configuration", "member_ids": ["B033-108"], "canonical_claim": "The new metadata storage can be selected directly with `metadata_type=content_addressed` without an `allow_experimental_*` gate.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/20260717_codex_review.md#major-severity"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3552", "topic": "capacity predicate boundaries", "target": "configuration", "member_ids": ["B040-031", "B040-055", "B040-068", "B040-074"], "canonical_claim": "The capacity contract must use independent predicates encoded_catalog <= catalog_object_cap and fold_fixed_bytes + sum(reservation) <= fold_object_cap, accepting equality and refusing cap plus one Additionally, The capacity tests must separately accept equality and refuse cap plus one for encoded catalog size and fold_fixed_bytes plus reservation sum, while keeping the other predicate slack Additionally, Each capacity predicate needs its own equality-acceptance and cap-plus-one refusal tests that assert which named predicate failed Additionally, The capacity fix independently tests equality acceptance and cap-plus-one refusal for each predicate while keeping the other predicate slack", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-28-ref-rework-reviews/codex_plans_r1_findings.md#L25-L27", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-28-ref-rework-reviews/codex_plans_r2_findings.md#L25-L27", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-28-ref-rework-reviews/codex_plans_r3_findings.md#L9-L10", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-28-ref-rework-reviews/codex_plans_r4_findings.md#L5-L5"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3553", "topic": "server root identity", "target": "configuration", "member_ids": ["B001-051", "B001-064", "B004-047"], "canonical_claim": "server_root_id must be a clean relative path without .., and two ClickHouse nodes must not share one server_root_id in the same pool. Additionally, server_root_id is required in the content-addressed disk configuration and is validated by Cas::validateServerRootId. Additionally, The `server_root_id` setting is required, immutable, and validated without sanitizing fallback; it roots `gc/server-roots/<srid>/`, `roots/<srid>/`, `cas/manifests/<srid>/`, and `staging/<srid>/`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/03-writer-protocol.md#L29-L43", "docs/superpowers/cas/11-walkthrough.md#server-root-id", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-12-cas-archaeology/01-frontend.md#L80-L94"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3554", "topic": "configuration", "target": "configuration", "member_ids": ["B003-076"], "canonical_claim": "The `system.content_addressed_log` audit is enabled by default by the `<content_addressed_log>` configuration section and costs no rows or construction when no CAS disk is configured.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/08-testing-and-soak.md#event-log"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3555", "topic": "configuration", "target": "configuration", "member_ids": ["B004-039", "B040-082", "B044-066"], "canonical_claim": "The `gc_shards` setting is fixed at pool creation and must be at least 1; it is not the same as the first-two-hex-digit S3 key sharding.; The persisted gc_shards value in cas_pool_meta is authoritative; a node reopening with a different local PoolConfig::gc_shards must use the persisted value; `gc_shards` defaults to 1, must be at least 1, and is creation-time-only because persisted GC state is authoritative on reopen.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/en/operations/storing-data.md#L520-L522", "docs/superpowers/cas/11-walkthrough.md#configuration", "docs/superpowers/cas/11-walkthrough.md#key-table", "docs/superpowers/cas/codecs.md#pool-metadata-capm"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3556", "topic": "conditional write size cap", "target": "configuration", "member_ids": ["B005-107", "B005-119", "B005-133"], "canonical_claim": "A generation-dialect CAS conditional write uses a single-part upload with the new `gcs_max_conditional_put_bytes` cap, defaulting to 1 GiB; a conditional write larger than the cap throws `NOT_IMPLEMENTED` and names the future Compose path and setting. Additionally, The generation-binding implementation's `gcs_max_conditional_put_bytes` cap buffers conditional single-PUT bodies in RAM; larger conditional writes fail rather than silently taking the multipart path.; The exact CA disk setting controlling the generation-store conditional single-PUT budget is `gcs_max_conditional_put_bytes`, with default `1ULL << 30`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-03-cas-gcs-generation-binding.md#global-constraints", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-03-cas-gcs-generation-binding.md#task-7-single-put-guard-for-conditional-writes", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-03-cas-gcs-generation-binding-design.md#conditional-writes-are-single-put-on-gcs"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3557", "topic": "configuration", "target": "configuration", "member_ids": ["B005-108", "B051-073"], "canonical_claim": "The new write settings for generation stores are `s3_force_single_part_upload` (default `false`) and `s3_single_part_upload_max_bytes_override` (default `0`, disabled); setting the former makes `WriteBufferFromS3` refuse multipart creation.; The CAS S3 write plumbing uses `s3_skip_check_objects_after_upload`, `s3_force_single_part_upload`, `s3_single_part_upload_max_bytes_override`, `s3_max_unexpected_write_error_retries_override`, and `s3_client_override` for mutable-key overwrite tolerance, GCS single-part requirements, and per-write retry policy.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/upstream-patch-inventory.md#write-settings-h", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-03-cas-gcs-generation-binding.md#global-constraints"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3558", "topic": "GCS generation dialect selection", "target": "configuration", "member_ids": ["B005-100", "B005-112", "B005-114"], "canonical_claim": "GCS generation-dialect mode is explicit: `http_client = gcp_oauth` enables the dialect for the existing OAuth client, and `http_client = gcs_hmac` selects `PocoHTTPClientGCSHMAC`; there is no endpoint auto-detection. Additionally, Without `http_client = gcs_hmac`, existing disks retain byte-identical wire behavior; GCS generation binding is explicit opt-in only. Additionally, `http_client = gcs_hmac` forces `ApiMode::GCS` even when credentials are present, because the SDK-side GCS accommodations must remain active for GOOG4 requests.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-03-cas-gcs-generation-binding.md#global-constraints", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-03-cas-gcs-generation-binding.md#task-3-pocohttpclientgcshmac-factory-selection-config-plumbing-apimodegcs-forcing", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-03-cas-gcs-generation-binding-design.md#mode-selection-explicit-opt-in-no-auto-detect"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3559", "topic": "configuration", "target": "configuration", "member_ids": ["B011-049"], "canonical_claim": "`PoolMeta.algos_used` is a canonically sorted, append-only set of every algorithm ever admitted to the pool; once an algorithm is admitted, subsequent opens with it need no flag.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-11-cas-mixed-algo-pools-design.md#poolmeta"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3560", "topic": "configuration", "target": "configuration", "member_ids": ["B011-050"], "canonical_claim": "The write algorithm is node-local `PoolConfig`/`Store` state and is not persisted as a single pool-wide value, because live nodes may intentionally write with different already-admitted algorithms.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-11-cas-mixed-algo-pools-design.md#poolmeta"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3561", "topic": "blob hash configuration", "target": "configuration", "member_ids": ["B011-048", "B011-064", "B011-065", "B019-070", "B044-063", "B044-064"], "canonical_claim": "A new algorithm is admitted only with explicit `<blob_hash_allow_new>1</blob_hash_allow_new>` opt-in; reopening with an unadmitted algorithm and no flag fails with `BAD_ARGUMENTS`. Additionally, The selectable blob hash defaults to `cityHash128` v1.0.2 and adds `xxh3-128` and `sha256`; the algorithm is encoded in blob paths and the feature is pre-release with no data migration. Additionally, The disk setting `blob_hash` accepts `cityhash128`, `xxh3-128`, or `sha256`; unknown values fail with `BAD_ARGUMENTS`, and Phase 1 rejects `sha256` with `NOT_IMPLEMENTED` until Phase 2. Additionally, Review finding \u211614 leaves the `CityHash128` default as a design decision: `sha256` is available for hostile shared-pool threat models, while same-trust-domain replicas retain the default under the current model.; `blob_hash` accepts `cityhash128` or `sha256`, and the pool records the choice so reopening with a disagreement fails closed. Additionally, `blob_hash_allow_new` defaults to `false` and must be enabled to admit a new blob-hash algorithm into an existing pool's recorded algorithm set.", "issue_ids": ["\u211614"], "sources": ["docs/en/operations/storing-data.md#L512-L514", "docs/en/operations/storing-data.md#L515-L517", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-11-cas-mixed-algo-pools.md#task-4", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-17-codex-review-triage.md#L33-L34", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-17-codex-review-triage.md#L415-L427", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-11-cas-mixed-algo-pools-design.md#poolmeta", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-11-cas-pluggable-blob-hash-design.md#config", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-11-cas-pluggable-blob-hash-design.md#title"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3562", "topic": "configuration", "target": "configuration", "member_ids": ["B011-107"], "canonical_claim": "A writer publishes a snapshot when log count or log bytes exceed thresholds, or after mount recovery exceeds a threshold; publication is off the mutation hot path and never blocks appends.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-11-cas-ref-table-snapshot-log-design.md#writer-snapshot-publication"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3563", "topic": "configuration", "target": "configuration", "member_ids": ["B011-124"], "canonical_claim": "The default `cas_staging_backend=local` path is byte-for-byte the existing `scratchPath()` path; it performs no capability probe and takes no S3 staging branch.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-11-cas-s3-native-staging.md#global-constraints", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-11-cas-s3-native-staging-design.md#config"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3564", "topic": "configuration", "target": "configuration", "member_ids": ["B015-018"], "canonical_claim": "The unclean-handover wait must satisfy `unclean handover wait >= all client timeouts + materialization_grace_ms`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-13-cas-ref-lease-exclusivity-rev6-design.md#t-mat"]}
