{"cluster_id": "C-3566", "topic": "configuration", "target": "configuration", "member_ids": ["B022-024"], "canonical_claim": "An explicit `use_fake_transaction=true` on a `content_addressed` disk silently selects per-file autocommit and removes the atomic manifest/ref commit point, so registration should reject it with `BAD_ARGUMENTS`.", "issue_ids": ["finding-4"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-20-umbrella-review-fixes.md#task-3-reject-explicit-use-fake-transaction-true-on-cas-keeper-disks", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-20-umbrella-review-cas-vs-antalya-26.6.md#major-issues"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3567", "topic": "configuration", "target": "configuration", "member_ids": ["B022-062"], "canonical_claim": "The refactored `ContentAddressedMetadataStorage` constructor takes the object-storage pointer, key-compatibility prefix, server UUID, disk name, global context, and `const ContentAddressedSettings &`, with positional header defaults removed.", "issue_ids": ["F4"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-21-consistency-findings-f1-f11.md#task-6-f4b-rewire-the-factory-and-collapse-the-constructor", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-21-consistency-findings-f1-f11-design.md#f4-settings-struct"]}
