{"cluster_id": "C-3571", "topic": "configuration", "target": "configuration", "member_ids": ["B033-043", "B046-047"], "canonical_claim": "The CAS server setting names are `cas_blob_upload_pool_size` and `cas_condemned_upload_memory_bytes`.; The server setting names are cas_blob_upload_pool_size and cas_condemned_upload_memory_bytes, and the system table is system.cas_mounts.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-03-cas-naming/t3-report.md#L14-L20", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-03-cas-naming-unification-design.md#scope-what-is-renamed"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3572", "topic": "legacy CAS settings removal", "target": "configuration", "member_ids": ["B006-025", "B033-044", "B047-045"], "canonical_claim": "The dead legacy disk-config keys `content_addressed_allow_shared_pool` and `content_addressed_gc_grace_sec` are not read and are removed from the skip-list and every configuration that sets them. Additionally, The legacy settings `<content_addressed_allow_shared_pool>` and `<content_addressed_gc_grace_sec>` were removed from CAS integration configs because unrecognized keys reach `impl->set` and raise an exception after Task 3 removed them from `non_cas_keys`.; The removed configuration keys `content_addressed_gc_grace_sec` and `content_addressed_allow_shared_pool` are not parsed and must not appear in soak configurations.", "issue_ids": ["T6"], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-03-cas-naming/t6-report.md#L8-L16", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-03-cas-naming-unification-design.md#scope-what-is-renamed", "docs/superpowers/worklogs/2026-07-03-real-s3-validation.md#L35-L36"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3573", "topic": "configuration", "target": "configuration", "member_ids": ["B033-048"], "canonical_claim": "Per-disk CAS settings such as `scratch_path`, `gc_enabled`, and `server_root_id` remain unprefixed because they are scoped by their disk block.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-03-cas-naming-unification.md#cas-naming-unification-implementation-plan"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3574", "topic": "CAS metadata type naming", "target": "configuration", "member_ids": ["B033-039", "B033-052", "B038-032", "B046-048", "B048-059"], "canonical_claim": "The accepted metadata storage type spelling is `cas`, and `system.disks.metadata_type` renders it as `CAS`. Additionally, The canonical metadata storage type is cas: metadataTypeFromString accepts cas, registration uses registerMetadataStorageType(\"cas\", \u2026), and unknown content_addressed fails with UNKNOWN_ELEMENT_IN_CONFIG rather than acting as an alias. Additionally, The current CAS metadata type is `cas`; the old `content_addressed` value, old config filename `content_addressed_*.xml`, and old stateless prefixes `content_addressed` and `ca_gc` are retired in favor of `cas_*`. Additionally, The metadata storage type string is changed from `content_addressed` to `cas`, and no compatibility alias is retained because the branch is unreleased.; A CAS disk is an `object_storage` disk with `metadata_type` set to `cas`; `<readonly>1</readonly>` disables mount-slot claims, capability probes, and writes.", "issue_ids": ["B31", "T8"], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-03-cas-naming/t3-report.md#L22-L43", ".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-03-cas-naming/t8-report.md#L13-L24", ".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-03-cas-naming/t8-report.md#L99-L116", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-03-cas-naming-unification.md#task-3-system-tables-server-settings-config-metadatatype", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-03-cas-naming-unification-design.md#goal", "src/Disks/DiskObjectStorage/MetadataStorages/ContentAddressed/README.md#configuration"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3575", "topic": "configuration", "target": "configuration", "member_ids": ["B033-053", "B046-046"], "canonical_claim": "The CAS system log configuration sections are `<cas_log>` and `<cas_gc_log>`, corresponding to the tables `system.cas_log` and `system.cas_gc_log`.; The CAS system-log members and their default table/config names are cas_gc_log and cas_log; CREATE_PUBLIC_MEMBERS stringifies the member name for both the default table name and the config prefix.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-03-cas-naming/t3-report.md#L3-L12", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-03-cas-naming-unification.md#task-3-system-tables-server-settings-config-metadatatype"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3576", "topic": "configuration", "target": "configuration", "member_ids": ["B014-036", "B015-109", "B033-059", "B044-067", "B047-012"], "canonical_claim": "The per-disk CAS settings are `deduplication_cache_bytes`, `deduplication_head_first_min_bytes`, and `gc_snapshot_generations_to_keep`.; The measured decision is to retain the factory default `dedup_cache_bytes` of 67108864 bytes (64 MiB); 256 MiB produced flat `CasBlobHead`, `CasBlobBodyPutAvoided`, PUT-class, and hit-rate results, so `MetadataStorageFactory.cpp:267` remains unchanged. Additionally, The Round-B plan defines `dedup_cache_bytes` as an existing cache setting with a documented 64 MiB default and proposes measuring 64 MiB, 256 MiB, and 1 GiB variants. Additionally, `deduplication_cache_bytes` defaults to 64 MiB, and `deduplication_head_first_min_bytes` defaults to 1 MiB with `0` disabling the pre-upload `HEAD`. Additionally, The CAS settings are named `deduplication_cache_bytes`, `deduplication_head_first_min_bytes`, and `gc_snapshot_generations_to_keep`; no compatibility alias for the former abbreviated names is provided.", "issue_ids": ["T5"], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-03-cas-obscure-names/t5-report.md#L15-L18", "docs/en/operations/storing-data.md#L523-L525", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-14-cas-opt-levers-s1-s5.md#task-3-2-dedup-cache-sizing-measurement-no-cas-code", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-03-cas-obscure-names-cleanup.md#task-5-per-disk-settings-and-test-names-dedup-gc-snap", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-13-cas-memory-s3-budget-optimizations-design.md#s2-dedup-cache"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3577", "topic": "configuration", "target": "configuration", "member_ids": ["B038-060"], "canonical_claim": "The known-present blob cache is a bounded cost hint: reducing `deduplication_cache_bytes` may lower `CASBlobDeduplicationCacheHit` but must not change correctness.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["utils/ca-soak/scenarios/README.md#s24-small-dedup-cache-capacity"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3578", "topic": "CAS functional test job placement", "target": "configuration", "member_ids": ["B040-003", "B040-010", "B040-011"], "canonical_claim": "All 10 CAS ParamSets belong in AltinityJobConfigs.cas_functional_tests_jobs rather than JobConfigs.functional_tests_jobs Additionally, The module-level FUNCTIONAL_TESTS_JOBS list concatenates JobConfigs.functional_tests_jobs with AltinityJobConfigs.cas_functional_tests_jobs Additionally, That FUNCTIONAL_TESTS_JOBS concatenation preserves the previous functional-test list element-for-element and in the same order because the CAS ParamSets were previously last", "issue_ids": [], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/ci-review-fixes-report.md#L13-L31", ".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/ci-review-fixes-report.md#L34-L55", ".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/ci-review-fixes-report.md#L48-L55"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3579", "topic": "configuration", "target": "configuration", "member_ids": ["B040-012"], "canonical_claim": "ci/jobs/functional_tests.py selects jobs using the --options parameter string rather than job objects", "issue_ids": [], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/ci-review-fixes-report.md#L55-L56"]}

